sequenceDiagram

actor Client
participant Server as server.js
participant Route as Mounted feature router
participant Auth as protect / authorize / approvedProvider
participant M as User / AuthSession / Provider
participant DB as MongoDB
participant C as Named feature controller
Client->>Server: Protected request + Authorization header
Server->>Route: Parse JSON, match method/path
Route->>Auth: protect(options)
activate Auth
Auth->>Auth: Verify JWT signature, expiry and subject
Auth->>M: Read user and active non-expired session
M->>DB: Scoped authentication reads
DB-->>Auth: Current role, provider and session
opt Provider role and not logout
    Auth->>M: Read current Provider status
    M->>DB: Check provider exists and is not suspended
end
Auth-->>Route: req.actor or next(error)
deactivate Auth
Route->>Route: Role guard, approval when required, input validation
Route->>C: req.actor + req.validated
alt GET /api/v1/auth/me
    C->>M: Read own User by actor.userId
    M->>DB: Read account
    C-->>Server: 200 serialized account
else POST /api/v1/auth/logout
    Note over Route,Auth: allowSuspended true, token/session must still be valid
    C->>M: Revoke only actor.sessionId for actor.userId
    M->>DB: Set revokedAt if active and unexpired
    C-->>Server: 200 logout message, or 401 if no active session
else Other protected operation
    C-->>Server: Feature response after its scoped work
end
Server-->>Client: JSON response
Note over Server,C: Validation/auth/domain failures use the shared handler, unexpected failures have a safe 500 message
